WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.063
Customers register, verify email, and sign in. Forgotten passwords can be reset. All accounts shown are synthetic.

2
00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:16.538
My orders shows your requests, progress, and next action. Open an order for its delivery tracker and update history.

3
00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:24.673
Choose Internet, SD-WAN, or Cloud Connect, then enter the site details and your preferred contact channel.

4
00:00:25.292 --> 00:00:32.874
Correct missing site information to release a hold. Profile manages contact preferences and your password.

5
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:40.165
Partners accept a staff invitation, choose a password, and sign in to their own organisation.

6
00:00:40.792 --> 00:00:50.306
Deliveries highlights expected dates, delays, and required actions. Update installation details and access notes to keep work moving.

7
00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:58.989
Payments shows outstanding, overdue, and paid invoices, with due dates and references. No money actually moves.

8
00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:06.673
Raise a delivery, billing, or technical concern, link an order, and follow the service team's replies.

9
00:01:07.292 --> 00:01:11.750
Service staff sign in with the access token on this deployment.

10
00:01:12.375 --> 00:01:23.051
The control tower summarises activations, exceptions, and recoveries. Order workspace opens each journey's execution history and tool
activity.

11
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:30.993
Exception desk brings route conflicts and change-window holds to people for explicit approval or rejection.

12
00:01:31.625 --> 00:01:39.816
Staff invite partners, create orders, manage billing terms, and resolve questions through the shared concerns inbox.

13
00:01:40.417 --> 00:01:55.817
Validate checks feasibility. Decompose plans service and resource work. Provision orchestrates tasks. Recover retries known faults.
Communicate sends updates. The supervisor coordinates handoffs; exceptions need people.

14
00:01:56.458 --> 00:02:10.879
Analytics measures delivery time, fallout, and agent bottlenecks. Compare live orders with isolated benchmarks against seven-day and
eight-percent targets. Synthetic timings are not real carrier performance.

15
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:20.587
Trust and governance explains safety boundaries and provenance, with an exportable audit trail. Service provisioning remains simulated.
